 "notes": "Hidden photon (dark photon) DM haloscope. Headline result: combined 95% CL exclusion on kinetic mixing chi vs hidden photon mass from resonant + broadband scans (Fig 19; resonant detail Fig 18). Curve traced as the lower (limit) boundary of the blue WISPDMX excluded region, which is embedded as a raster image (I1) inside the vector PDF of Fig 19; axis calibrated from the vector spines/tick labels (x=log10(m/eV) in [-10,0], y=log10(chi) in [-16,-4]). Mass converted from frequency via m=4.13567 ueV*(nu/GHz); range 0.4 neV (4e-10 eV) to 2.07 ueV. Broadband limit ~1e-12; deep resonant dips ~4e-14 at TM010 (0.86 ueV), TE111 (1.33 ueV), TM020 (1.9 ueV); limit steadily weakens below ~0.2 ueV. rho_DM=0.3 GeV/cm^3 assumed (paper native, not rescaled). chi reported directly (not chi^2).",
